Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 01:13:56 +0000

Emacs read the jj maildir and posted by writing into it, so a post
reached the list only when it was committed and pushed. Through
lab-mail it is posted at once, and Pat reads the same folders as
Fastmail and every other client.

- notmuch uses the lab-mail profile.
- Mail goes out through msmtp, and an Fcc copy in the local sent
  folder shows it as sent before the next sync.
- M i, M n, M l, and M a move the message or thread at point to
  INBOX, Next, Later, or Archive. The folder is the state, so a tag
  alone would be undone by the next notmuch new.
- Saved searches for inbox, next, and later.
